reply.analysis:
All 6 round-1 trials scored 0 on dev and 0 on training success. Earlier searches add about 84 more zeros, so there is still no evidence for or against any idea. The agent never completes an exact build even in training. So the bottleneck is optimisation or inductive bias, not generalisation. Round 1 stacked init hygiene, GroupNorm, skips, factorised heads, landing gating, GLU heads, 3x3 type convs and recipe extremes; none worked. Round 2 keeps going for breadth with families not yet tried:
- token-mixing (MLP-Mixer) global context;
- a myopic recipe (gamma 0.9, lambda 0.8) with 1 epoch, which leans on the dense per-placement reward;
- hierarchical type-then-anchor log-softmax factorisation;
- a recurrent bottom-up and top-down scan over layers, with shared gated 2D convs, to learn the landing layer;
- a bilinear (multiplicative) stem with a footprint head that concatenates per-cell features instead of pooling them;
- a sample-heavy "everything" stack.

All keep r at or below about 1.4 and use no 3D convolutions.
